Description: [Max 500 words: impact (location, beneficiary numbers, expected outcomes); any additional points to raise; show link with CO&#x2019;s country strategy]_x000d_
The project aims to support crisis-affected children, adolescents with and without disabilities and caregivers&#x2019; wellbeing through the provision of MHPSS services and information on childcare and protection, including SGBV and ASRH services. Additionally, the project will strengthen referral mechanisms and multisectoral coordination to improve quality and access to services and respond to violence against children (VAC) of different sex, age, diversity and disabilities. In the face of multiple crises and high protection risks there is need to address the capacity gaps of service providers, particularly in providing inclusive MHPSS, SGBV and SRH, supporting social workers, health providers and other service providers to respond adequately to the needs and provide accessible and quality services to the girls, and boys and adolescents in the districts of Erati and Meconta, Nampula district, as part of the current IDP crisis in the northern of Mozambique._x000d_
Project Outputs:_x000d_
&#x2022; Provision of screening and family tracing and reunification services, including alternative care, for IDPs affected by attacks in Er&#xe1;ti._x000d_
&#x2022; Capacity of CP Case Management Service Provider is strengthened in order to engage meaningfully in the promotion and provision of MHPSS at family and community level._x000d_
&#x2022; Provision of MHPSS support for persons affected by the conflict in northern Moz, Er&#xe1;ti &amp; Corrane_x000d_
&#x2022; Mitigation of GBV risks for persons impacted by the conflict in Northern Mozambique, Er&#xe1;ti &amp; Corrane._x000d_
&#x2022; Community ownership and active participation through Community Engagement, Accountability to Affected Population, Safeguarding and PSHEA Activities.</narrative>
  </description>
